## XIOM in the Browser

```sh
# Build for WASM
xiom build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown

# Build with WASM bindings (for JS interop)
xiom build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --wasm-bindgen

# Optimize for size
xiom build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release -Os
```

### Simple WASM Module

```xiom
// lib.xi — compiled to WASM
#[no_mangle]
pub fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {
  return a + b;
}

#[no_mangle]
pub fn fibonacci(n: Int) -> Int {
  if n <= 1 { return n; }
  return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}
```

### JavaScript Interop

```javascript
// Load and use the WASM module
const xiom = await WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(
  fetch('lib.wasm')
);

const { add, fibonacci } = xiom.instance.exports;
console.log(add(40, 2));        // 42
console.log(fibonacci(10));     // 55
```

### WASM Bindings

```xiom
// With --wasm-bindgen, use higher-level interop
#[wasm_bindgen]
pub fn greet(name: Str) -> Str {
  return "Hello, " + name + "!";
}

#[wasm_bindgen]
pub type Counter = {
  value: Int;
}

#[wasm_bindgen]
impl Counter {
  pub fn new() -> Counter { return Counter{ value: 0 }; }
  pub fn increment(self: &mut Counter) { self.value = self.value + 1; }
  pub fn get(self: &Counter) -> Int { return self.value; }
}
```

### JavaScript Side

```javascript
import init, { greet, Counter } from './pkg/myapp.js';

await init();
console.log(greet('Kilo'));        // Hello, Kilo!

const counter = Counter.new();
counter.increment();
counter.increment();
console.log(counter.get());        // 2
```

### WASM Use Cases

- **Computation-heavy tasks**: image processing, cryptography, physics simulation
- **Code reuse**: share business logic between backend and frontend
- **Performance**: near-native speed in the browser
- **Sandboxing**: WASM provides a secure sandbox by default

### Size Optimization

```sh
# Minimal WASM binary
xiom build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release -Oz --no-default-libs

# Analyze size
xiom size target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/lib.wasm
```

